From fa2a8cffa69c303fd1c3df7bd5755c5232d87493 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kingshukbanu1987-beep
 <329612224+kingshukbanu1987-beep@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:26:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Store First name, Last name and State from the registration
 form

The registration page has always collected First name, Last name and State,
and the Users table has dedicated FirstName / LastName / State columns for
them, but POST /api/registration never accepted or wrote those values: the
request DTO only carried FullName, so the three columns stayed NULL and the
profile page could not show the state or the separate names.

* RegistrationRequest gains FirstName / LastName / State (multipart fields
  firstName / lastName / state, max 100 chars each).
* RegistrationController writes them to the member row; a name part a client
  does not post is split out of FullName ("Kingshuk Banu" -> Kingshuk /
  Banu, "Ana Maria Lopez" with FirstName "Ana Maria" -> Lopez), so older
  clients fill the columns too.
* AuthController stores the provider's given_name / family_name (Google)
  on the Pending row created by the OAuth login.
* ProfileDto answers FirstName / LastName / State, ProfileMapper fills them
  (splitting FullName for rows whose columns are still empty) and
  UpdateProfileRequest / PUT /api/profile accept the same three fields.
* README documents the fields and the split fallback.
* neverbeen-api-registration-names-state-verification.py ports the helpers
  and checks the payloads end to end (no .NET SDK in the build sandbox).
